<table width="100%">
<tr>
<td><font size="+2"><B><A HREF="/Xpilot/Maps/actvolcano.xp">Active Volcano</A></B>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <font color="#FF0000">T</font></font></td>
<td ALIGN=RIGHT>by <a href="mailto:pad53945@sci.tamucc.edu?subject=Active%20Volcano">Zemyla</a></td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td COLSPAN="2"><img SRC="/Xpilot/Maps/actvolcano.gif" ALT="Active Volcano" HSPACE=5 height=100 width=200 align=LEFT>
This is like my regular Volcano map, except that the crater now has been taken up by asteroid concentrators (need 4.5.0 or better) that shoot asteroids into the air. &nbsp;You get items by blasting asteroids open (need 4.4.2 or better). &nbsp;Getting a ball to the other side is interesting, because if it hits an asteroid, it is destroyed; your best bet is to use phasing or hyperjumps.<BR><BR>As you may have noticed, this is a rather new-fangled map :-).<BR>
</td>
</tr>
</table>

